From e88ffc4d16b96d58374d5b2dbb8e9145463a4a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:19:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: fix a stored XSS in the client-picker dropdown, and drop
 the last shipped ASUS URL

Two backlog [P3] items. The first turned out to be worse than filed.

1. CLIENT-PICKER DROPDOWN - STORED XSS, NOT THE COSMETIC RESIDUAL ON THE LIST.
The backlog described the remainder as defense-in-depth on vendor/deviceTypeName
tooltips. Those are in fact already encoded (v2.2.0), and every htmlEncode in the
tree does escape the apostrophe, so that part was already done. The real residual
is one layer over, in showDropdownClientList()/genClientItem():

    code += '<div onclick="' + _callBackFun + '(\''
    code += getClientValue(param[j], clientObj);      <-- device NAME, raw
    code += '\');">'

A value there crosses TWO parsers: the HTML attribute decoder runs first, then
JS. HTML-encoding is therefore NOT protection in that position - and the client
list is HTML-encoded at ingestion (v2.1.3), so a DHCP hostname of

    x');<payload>;//

is stored as  x&#39;);<payload>;//  , the attribute decoder turns &#39; back into
an apostrophe, the JS string closes early, and the payload is code. Proven in a
browser, not by reading: with the callback defined as the real pages define it,
the injected statement EXECUTED on click; with the fix it does not, and the
onclick reads setClientIP('x\');...') - one string argument. (An earlier run that
looked safe was a false negative: the harness had not defined the callback, so
the first call threw and aborted the rest of the handler.)

Reach: any LAN device can set its own DHCP hostname; ~20 shipped pages mount this
dropdown (QoS, Parental Controls, VPN Director, Virtual Server, DNS Director,
Key Guard, TOR, ACL, Guest Network, System...), and the ones passing 'name>mac'
put the name straight into the handler. Click-gated on the admin, but stored.

FIX: jsAttrArg() - decode to the raw text, escape THAT for a JS single-quoted
string, then HTML-encode the result so the attribute stays well formed. Applied
to every value that lands inside an inline handler; the <a id=/title= pair is now
quoted and encoded too.

Same function, same root cause, cosmetic half: clientName was sliced at 30 chars
while HTML-ENCODED, so a cut could land inside an entity (&#39; -> &#3) and
render as garble - the "garble" half of the original report. clipEncodedName()
slices the decoded text and re-encodes. Measured: old 'aaa...&#..', new
'aaa...&#39;b..'.

2. DE-CLOUD - THE LAST REQUEST-SHAPED ASUS URL IN THE IMAGE IS GONE.
clientlist.module.js still carried the v2.2.0 cloud icon-catalogue fetch, dead
behind an early return but present in the shipped bytes and reading as live to
anyone grepping the firmware. Body removed; the comment explaining why stays.

The backlog's other half asked for a per-model shipping check before sweeping the
~133 ASUS URLs left in sysdep/FUNCTION/{ROG_UI,TUF_UI,UI4,GS_UI}. Done, and the
answer is that sweeping is the wrong move: www/Makefile gates each of those
overlays on an RTCONFIG flag, and NOTHING in this tree sets ROG_UI, TUF_UI,
RT_TUF_UI, GS_UI, UI4 or TS_UI to y - they are dead for all five models. Editing
133 lines of upstream-pristine source that never ships would only add patch-series
noise. What was missing is the guarantee, so that is now a build gate instead:
reaper_verify check 17 fails the build if any ASUS-CDN reference reaches the
STAGED www in a request-shaped position (fetch/XHR/ajax/getJSON/new Image/.src=/
script|img src=/link href=). A future model that enables one of those overlays
stops the build rather than silently reintroducing the surface.

Deliberately NOT gated: plain href / openLink / window.open links to ASUS support
pages - user-initiated navigation, not a silent callback. The shipped stock pages
carry ~170 of those (FAQ, policy, support); removing them is a separate product
decision, not a privacy fix, and is left to the owner.

Gate tested both ways: it flags fetch(), <img src=> and .src= to an ASUS host,
stays quiet on href/openLink links, and reports zero hits across the shipping
source www.

NOT BUILT. The XSS fix wants an on-device check: set a hostile DHCP hostname on a
LAN device, open a page with the client dropdown, confirm the name renders as
text and clicking it still selects the client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/client_function.js     | 40 ++++++++++++++-----
 .../www/dashboard/js/clientlist.module.js     | 18 ++++-----
 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/client_function.js b/release/src/router/www/client_function.js
index 79141077e1..c876b6f73e 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/client_function.js
+++ b/release/src/router/www/client_function.js
@@ -3853,6 +3853,31 @@ function control_dropdown_client_block(_containerID, _pullArrowID, _evt) {
 	}
 }
 
+/* reaper: a value that lands INSIDE onclick="fn('...')" crosses TWO parsers -
+ * the HTML attribute decoder runs first, then JS. HTML-encoding alone is
+ * therefore NOT protection in that position, which is the trap this dropdown
+ * fell into: clientList names are HTML-encoded at ingestion (see genClientList),
+ * so a DHCP hostname of  x');...;//  is stored as  x&#39;);...;//  , the
+ * attribute decoder turns it back into an apostrophe, and the JS string closes
+ * early. Verified in a browser: the payload ran on click.
+ * Decode to the raw text, escape THAT for a JS single-quoted string, then
+ * HTML-encode the result so the attribute itself stays well formed. */
+function jsAttrArg(_value) {
+	var raw = htmlEnDeCode.htmlDecode(String((_value == null) ? "" : _value));
+	raw = raw.replace(/\\/g, "\\\\").replace(/'/g, "\\'").replace(/[\r\n\u2028\u2029]/g, " ");
+	return htmlEnDeCode.htmlEncode(raw);
+}
+
+/* reaper: the stored name is HTML-ENCODED, so slicing it by character count can
+ * cut an entity in half (&#39; -> &#3) and render as garble. Slice the decoded
+ * text, then re-encode. */
+function clipEncodedName(_value, _max) {
+	var raw = htmlEnDeCode.htmlDecode(String((_value == null) ? "" : _value));
+	if(raw.length > _max)
+		raw = raw.substring(0, _max - 2) + "..";
+	return htmlEnDeCode.htmlEncode(raw);
+}
+
 //_callBackFunParam = mac>ip>..., _interfaceMode = all(wired, wll), wired, wl, _clientState = all, online, offline
 function showDropdownClientList(_callBackFun, _callBackFunParam, _interfaceMode, _containerID, _pullArrowID, _clientState) {
 	document.body.addEventListener("click", function(_evt) {control_dropdown_client_block(_containerID, _pullArrowID, _evt);})
@@ -3898,31 +3923,26 @@ function showDropdownClientList(_callBackFun, _callBackFunParam, _interfaceMode,
 		var code = "";
 		var clientName = (clientObj.nickName == "") ? clientObj.name : clientObj.nickName;
 		
-		code += '<a id=' + clientList[i] + ' title=' + clientList[i] + '>';
+		code += '<a id="' + htmlEnDeCode.htmlEncode(clientList[i]) + '" title="' + htmlEnDeCode.htmlEncode(clientList[i]) + '">';
 		if(_state == "online")
 			code += '<div onclick="' + _callBackFun + '(\'';
 		else if(_state == "offline")
 			code += '<div style="color:#A0A0A0" onclick="' + _callBackFun + '(\'';
 		for(var j = 0; j < param.length; j += 1) {
 			if(j == 0) {
-				code += getClientValue(param[j], clientObj);
+				code += jsAttrArg(getClientValue(param[j], clientObj));
 			}
 			else {
 				code += '\', \'';
-				code += getClientValue(param[j], clientObj);
+				code += jsAttrArg(getClientValue(param[j], clientObj));
 			}
 		}
 		code += '\');">';
 		code += '<strong>';
-		if(clientName.length > 32) {
-			code += clientName.substring(0, 30) + "..";
-		}
-		else {
-			code += clientName;
-		}
+		code += clipEncodedName(clientName, 32);
 		code += '</strong>';
 		if(_state == "offline")
-			code += '<strong title="Remove this client" style="float:right;margin-right:5px;cursor:pointer;" onclick="removeClient(\'' + clientObj.mac + '\', \'' + _containerID  + '_clientlist_dropdown_expand\', \'' + _containerID  + '_clientlist_offline\')">&times;</strong>';
+			code += '<strong title="Remove this client" style="float:right;margin-right:5px;cursor:pointer;" onclick="removeClient(\'' + jsAttrArg(clientObj.mac) + '\', \'' + jsAttrArg(_containerID)  + '_clientlist_dropdown_expand\', \'' + jsAttrArg(_containerID)  + '_clientlist_offline\')">&times;</strong>';
 		code += '</div><!--[if lte IE 6.5]><iframe class="hackiframe2"></iframe><![endif]--></a>';
 		return code;
 	};
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/dashboard/js/clientlist.module.js b/release/src/router/www/dashboard/js/clientlist.module.js
index 9a76f3c03c..9ea283656b 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/dashboard/js/clientlist.module.js
+++ b/release/src/router/www/dashboard/js/clientlist.module.js
@@ -7927,18 +7927,16 @@ class ClinetIconFetcher {
 
     async fetchIconList() {
         /* reaper de-cloud (v2.2.0, backlog item): no browser->ASUS-CDN requests.
-           This replaced the bundled icon catalog above with a cloud copy from
-           nw-dlcdnet.asus.com on every client-popup open. The constructor's
+           This used to replace the bundled icon catalog above with a cloud copy
+           from nw-dlcdnet.asus.com on every client-popup open. The constructor's
            built-in list stays authoritative; getIconByType/queryIconList work
-           unchanged against it. */
+           unchanged against it.
+           2026-08-11: the dead fetch body is REMOVED, not just short-circuited
+           behind the early return. It shipped an ASUS URL in the image, it read
+           as a live call to anyone grepping the firmware, and it was the only
+           request-shaped ASUS reference left in the staged www - which is now a
+           build gate (reaper_verify check 17). */
         return;
-
-        const response = await fetch('https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/beta/plugin/js/extend_custom_svg_icon.json')
-            .then(res => res.json())
-            .then(data => {
-                this.iconList = data;
-                this.iconList.source = "cloud";
-            });
     }
 
     getIconList() {
